                "Half of a reading is the question. The best questions are open and about you: \"What do I need to understand about this relationship?\" instead of \"Does he love me?\".\n\nAsk about what you can influence: \"How can I prepare for the interview?\" works better than \"Will I get the job?\".\n\nFor quick decisions use the Yes or No spread, but take the answer as a hint, not an order.\n\nBefore drawing, take a breath, phrase the question in one sentence, and don't ask the same thing again and again — the first answer is usually the most honest.",
